body:
**Clause:** IEEE 1800-2017 §7.8.5 (p.156); IEEE 1800-2023 §7.8.5 (p.165).

**Normative requirement:** "Declared indices shall have the equality operator defined for its type to be legal." §7.8.5 shows an unpacked struct used as an associative-array index type. A struct of byte/int members has equality defined.

**Probe:** tests/1800_audit/c07/ split file a4 (evidence: evidence/ieee1800-audit-c07c-20261020/attempt-03-assoc-split/, local build of exact cc25756d1 source; the same crash appears in Linux Slurm job 3515):
```systemverilog
typedef struct { byte B; int I; } U;
int au[U]; U u1, u2, u3;
initial begin
  $display("BEGIN a4"); $fflush;
  u1 = '{1,10}; u2 = '{2,20}; u3 = '{1,11};
  au[u1] = 5; au[u2] = 6;
  $display("A4 %0d %0d %0d", au.size(), au[u1], au.exists(u3));
end
```
Compile rc=0. At runtime, `BEGIN a4` prints and then vvp crashes: -g2017 rc 139 (SIGSEGV), -g2023 rc 138 (SIGBUS). No result line is printed.

**Controls (pass in both editions):** class-handle keys (`A1 2 1 2`), derived-class key (`A2 3 3`), null class key (`A3 1 4`, §7.8.3 "A null index is valid"), associative-array assignment copy (`A5 1 9`), by-value/ref passing (`1`, `200`), and the incompatible-formal diagnostics.

**Expected:** `A4 2 5 0` in both editions. If an index type were unsupported, the expected result would be a compile-time diagnostic, never a runtime crash.

**Dedupe:** open+closed searches for associative-array class/struct index, null index, associative argument, 7.8.3, 7.9.10, and crash/segfault terms. Reviewed #429, #484, #485, #734, #801, #803 and closed #44; none covers a struct-index crash.

## Summary

A 256-bit explicit value-range bin in a coverpoint fails elaboration on current Icarus main. A 64-bit range with the same form compiles and runs. This blocks the M20 SoC-IFC rows after their run-local coverage overlay converts wildcard/alignment bins to exact ranges.

## Reproducer

```systemverilog
module wide_explicit_range;
  covergroup cg with function sample(input bit [255:0] value);
    cp: coverpoint value { bins full = {[256'h0:256'hffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff]}; }
  endgroup
  cg coverage = new();
  initial begin
    coverage.sample('0);
    $display("WIDE_EXPLICIT_RANGE_OK");
    $finish;
  end
endmodule
```

## Expected and observed

Expected: compile and run to `WIDE_EXPLICIT_RANGE_OK`, consistent with the explicit coverpoint-bin value-range syntax in IEEE 1800-2017 §19.5.1.

Observed on Icarus 13.0 devel, source `cc25756d187314742d347267c2a513b3e640a7fb`, `iverilog` SHA-256 `87bb417df23d260bcfde3fb372b4a80eaad69e4fd2eea1ffb8b0eff10f7af08e`: compile exits 1 with `wide covergroup bin 'full' requires unsigned packed exact constant values (up to 256 bits); the bin cannot be represented.` The paired 64-bit control compiles and runs to `NARROW_EXPLICIT_RANGE_OK`.

Affected Caliptra M20 rows: 0–4 and 43–45. The reproducer, control, full compiler logs, and hashes are preserved in QD-BFM M21 evidence.

### Clause
- IEEE Std 1800-2017: §19.6 Defining cross coverage (p. 572)
- IEEE Std 1800-2023: §19.6 Defining cross coverage (p. 599)

### Normative requirement (quoted <=40 words)
"Coverage points defined in a coverage group other than the one enclosing the cross cannot participate in a cross. Attempts to cross items from different coverage groups shall result in a compiler error."

### Runner probe and observed result
Probe file: `tests/1800_audit/c19/neg/n19_06_cross_other_cg_hier.sv`

```systemverilog
module test_other_cg_hier;
  bit a, b;
  covergroup first;
    ca: coverpoint a;
  endgroup
  first one = new;
  covergroup second;
    cb: coverpoint b;
    invalid: cross one.ca, cb; // ILLEGAL: cross item from another covergroup instance
  endgroup
  second two = new;
endmodule
```

Observed result:
On Slurm job 2991 (pinned main toolchain), compiling with `iverilog -g2017 -tnull` and `iverilog -g2023 -tnull` exits with code 0 and empty stderr. The compiler accepts the hierarchical cross item `one.ca` and creates an implicit coverpoint instead of diagnosing a compiler error.

### Expected behavior
The compiler must reject attempts to cross items from different coverage groups with a fatal compiler error in both IEEE 1800-2017 and IEEE 1800-2023 modes.

Caliptra generated UVMF configuration initializes a dynamic-array property from a one-element slice of a dynamic-array argument. The exact form occurs in `kv_env_configuration.svh` (lines 209–210) and `mldsa_env_configuration.svh` (lines 120–121):

```systemverilog
qvip_ahb_lite_slave_subenv_interface_names    = new[1];
qvip_ahb_lite_slave_subenv_interface_activity = new[1];
qvip_ahb_lite_slave_subenv_interface_names    = interface_names[0:0];
qvip_ahb_lite_slave_subenv_interface_activity = interface_activity[0:0];
```

The minimized class-level reproducer in the accompanying report uses the same dynamic-array formal arguments, class properties, enum activity type, allocation, and assignments. On the pinned Icarus 13.0 build (source `9b5fad2afb4104caa816b257d5bccc40f01b8c66`, binary SHA-256 `6cd9749cb1e981820f64fdc737ae458bf6c46e3fcad8927afaf92649ee9a3288`), `iverilog -g2017` rejects both slice assignments with `sorry: dynamic-array slice r-values are not yet supported as fixed-size unpacked-array expressions.` Verilator 5.032 rejects the same two expressions with `Illegal range select`.

A control that changes only the two assignments to indexed element copies compiles and runs on both tools, printing `DYNAMIC_ARRAY_CLASS_CONTROL_OK`. This is therefore a reproduced simulator support gap, but not an Icarus-only compatibility difference. Please classify whether Icarus should support this dynamic-array slice expression; no claim is made here about Verilator behavior beyond the observed 5.032 result.

Reproducer and control: `evidence/caliptra-bfm-m16-20261018/diagnostics/icarus-dynamic-array-slice/source/`. Slurm evidence archives for jobs 2786, 2787, and 2789 preserve source hashes, commands, raw output, and resource logs.

## Reduced reproducer

```systemverilog
package mvc_types_pkg;
  class mvc_sequence_item_base;
  endclass

  class ahb_master_burst_transfer extends mvc_sequence_item_base;
    bit RnW;
    bit [31:0] address;
    bit [2:0] size;
    bit [63:0] data[$];
    bit [1:0] resp[$];
  endclass
endpackage

package qvip_compat_pkg;
  import mvc_types_pkg::*;

  class ahb_reg_predictor #(type T = ahb_master_burst_transfer);
    virtual function void write(mvc_sequence_item_base tr);
      T transfer;
      T beat;
      if (!$cast(transfer, tr)) return;
      beat = new();
      beat.RnW = transfer.RnW;
      beat.size = transfer.size;
      for (int unsigned i = 0; i < transfer.data.size(); i++) begin
        beat.address = transfer.address + (i * (1 << transfer.size));
        beat.data.delete();
        beat.data.push_back(transfer.data[i]);
        beat.resp.delete();
        beat.resp.push_back(transfer.resp[i]);
      end
    endfunction
  endclass

  class pv_ahb_reg_predictor #(type T = int)
    extends ahb_reg_predictor #(.T(T));
    virtual function void write(mvc_sequence_item_base tr);
      T ahb_txn;
      $cast(ahb_txn, tr);
      if (ahb_txn.RnW && ahb_txn.address == 32'h1000)
        $display("PV_WRITE %h %h", ahb_txn.address, ahb_txn.data[0]);
    endfunction
  endclass
endpackage

module pv_generic_transfer_repro;
  import mvc_types_pkg::*;
  import qvip_compat_pkg::*;

  ahb_master_burst_transfer transfer;
  pv_ahb_reg_predictor #(ahb_master_burst_transfer) predictor;

  initial begin
    transfer = new();
    predictor = new();
    transfer.RnW = 1;
    transfer.address = 32'h1000;
    transfer.data.push_back(64'h1234);
    transfer.resp.push_back(2'b00);
    predictor.write(transfer);
    $finish;
  end
endmodule
```

Run with the pinned compiler:

```sh
iverilog -g2012 -s pv_generic_transfer_repro -o repro.vvp pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv
vvp -n repro.vvp
```

## Observed

Icarus 13.0 devel, source `9b5fad2afb4104caa816b257d5bccc40f01b8c66`, exits 10 during elaboration. The runtime does not start.

```text
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:40: error: Variable ahb_txn does not have a field named: RnW.
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:40: error: Variable ahb_txn does not have a field named: address.
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:23: error: `beat' has no member `RnW' (after an earlier error on this name).
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:24: error: `beat' has no member `size' (after an earlier error on this name).
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:26: error: `beat' has no member `address' (after an earlier error on this name).
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:27: error: Enable of unknown task ``beat.data.delete''.
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:28: error: Enable of unknown task ``beat.data.push_back''.
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:29: error: Enable of unknown task ``beat.resp.delete''.
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:30: error: Enable of unknown task ``beat.resp.push_back''.
/home/dsell/slurm-runs/caliptra-bfm/a2/m16-ahb-pv-generic-transfer-20261018-01/pv_generic_transfer_repro.sv:25: error: Object qvip_compat_pkg._ivl_0.write.transfer has no method "data.size(...)".
```

## Comparison

Verilator 5.051 devel (`v5.050-196-g7dcd4e0b6`) compiles and runs the same source, printing:

```text
PV_WRITE 00001000 0000000000001234
```

## Caliptra origin

The reduced inheritance pattern comes from the pinned generated PV environment. `pv_ahb_reg_predictor #(type T = int)` extends `ahb_reg_predictor #(.T(T))`; the generated specialization passes `ahb_reg_transfer_t`, a parameterized `ahb_master_burst_transfer` declaring `RnW`, `address`, `size`, `data[$]`, and `resp[$]`. Icarus reports those members missing in both the generated predictor and the QD-BFM predictor. The original PV row 46 compile log and reduced run capture are in `evidence/caliptra-bfm-m16-20261018/attempts/gate-2670-pv-ahb/` and `evidence/caliptra-bfm-m16-20261018/diagnostics/ahb-pv-generic-transfer/`.

Please classify whether this legal-looking inherited class type-parameter/member-access pattern is a simulator defect and fix it if appropriate. No upstream issue was opened.
